  <p class="eyebrow">Computer Architecture Dossier</p>
  <h1>Transmeta Crusoe</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Transmeta Crusoe was a low power processor designed to run x86 
    software using a VLIW architecture and Code Morphing Software to translate x86 instructions into native code. 
    It delivered x86 compatibility with much lower power consumption but failed to achieve success because of its performance.
  </p>

